You cannot sacrifice but on an altar. Some messages will indicate that
your luck has gone up.

>    Still have to find the spell shop :). Didn't find a sink either,
> still wouldn't dropping a ring into a sink make the ring disappear?

Yes, so only use this identifying trick with rings you have a spare one
of.

> Engraving helped me identify one wand as it made the bugs on the
> floor speed up -- thanks for the hint!

See my other reply for a little bit more information.

>    I gave up trying on all the armour, because it was cursed so often.
> Perhaps I should only put it on when my pet likes it.

That is another way of finding out whether things are cursed: your pet
will not usually step on them, and if it does, it will do so only
"reluctantly". No need to have it pick them up: if it steps on them,
they're not cursed (unless it did so to eat something).

The other, more certain, way is to drop things on an altar.

>> it will take a long time to forget the spells.  leave most the sutff
>> in a chest somewhere(it would probably be good to do it near the
>> altar on dl11)

>    Do you mean my altar on DL 1 or is there another one (fixed) on
> DL 11?

There are only a few fixed altars in the dungeon. The one in Mine Town
is the first you'll normally encounter. The second fixed one is normally
around level 26 or so (but you don't want to pray or sacrifice there!).

>    I'll try to find a chest and then bring most of my stuff into one
> place then and then lock it in a chest. Can I lock it with the
> key that I unlock doors with?

Yes. One size fits all. If you identify your key, it'll show up as a
skeleton key.

>    OK. I was only afraid when my cat started to mess with the guards
> in Minetown. I am constantly hoping it knows what it's doing and won't
> aim too high :).

It usually stops attacking if the creature it's fighting with may kill
it in one round. The Minetown Captain is an exception to this, since it
uses weapons to fight with, and only its barehanded damage is taken into
account when your pet decides if it will attack.

